00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:18,780
A Skull Dice Trap card!

259
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:20,648
Is this some kind of trick?

260
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:21,820
Don't cheat me!

261
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:26,877
Skull dice reduces your monster's attack
strength depending on the roll of the die.

262
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:30,842
The higher the number, the more
your monster's points are reduced.

263
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,730
No!

264
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:36,765
And now that your monster's
basically a wimp, swordsman, attack!

265
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:40,630
Ah!

266
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:45,677
Looks like your psychic
friends dropped the ball.

267
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:48,160
I only had one graceful dice card.

268
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:52,657
You've been getting some bum
information, and now I know why.

269
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:54,417
Because of how I held my cards,

270
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:58,157
you knew I had two dice cards,
but you couldn't tell which ones.

271
00:13:58,240 --> 00:14:00,940
Which means your ESP game was just a con.

272
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:02,817
You couldn't see my cards at all.

273
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:07,371
But I'll bet you got friends in high
places who can, you snake in the grass.

274
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:09,220
You cheat!

275
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:10,660
Uh-oh, busted.

276
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:12,440
Nice work, Joey.

277
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:13,914
Now you're in control.

278
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:17,760
Violation! Run!

279
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,200
Freeze! Gotcha!

280
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:27,177
Your brother will never
duel in this town again.

281
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:28,417
We've learned our lesson.

282
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:30,477
Please, you've got to
give him another chance.

283
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:34,977
As the Battle City Tournament Commissioner,
it's my swarm duty to bust cheaters.

284
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:37,837
Give me one good reason why
I shouldn't cancel this duel.

285
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:38,977
You just can't.

286
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:40,357
Show some mercy, Commish.

287
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,637
Our brother isn't doing
this for the dueling glory.

288
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,955
He's doing it for us.

289
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:47,045
We're carnival folk, or
at least we used to be.

290
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:50,597
Since we left the show, he's
kept the bullies off our backs.

291
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:53,209
Your big brother protects
you from bullies?

292
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:56,269
That reminds me of when
I was a little kid.

293
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,640
Oh, does the baby need a diaper? Yeah.

294
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:02,796
Why don't you guys try picking on me?

295
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:07,237
See, every day after school, the
big kids would gang up on us.

296
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:10,117
But even bullies respect a
good duelist like our brother.

297
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,553
As long as he wins, they leave us alone.

298
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:15,034
We're just trying to make sure he does.

299
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:17,410
It's Yugi!

300
00:15:17,493 --> 00:15:19,160
He must have seen everything.

301
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,080
It's still cheating!

302
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:27,097
If I let you guys off the hook, what's to
stop you from pulling this stunt again?

303
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:28,010
I'm begging.

304
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:31,084
Let my brother duel or
we're toast after school.

305
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:33,957
Just give him a chance to go legit.

306
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:37,216
Espa may be a bogus psychic,
but he's a great duelist!

307
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:45,420
They seem sincere, I bet Yu-Gi
would give him a second chance.

308
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:47,160
What do you say?

309
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,840
Come on, have a heart.

310
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,560
This is your last chance.

311
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,917
If he cheats again, then it's no more Mr.

312
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,560
Nice Guy. Thanks, Kamish.

313
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:02,260
Big brother stories get me every time.

314
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:06,080
I haven't seen Yu-Gi all day.

315
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:11,159
I hope that everything's all right.

316
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:17,837
Ishizu said he had to enter this tournament
to save the world from an ancient evil.

317
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:20,391
But who knows when that evil will show up?

318
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:25,260
All I know for sure is that when it
does, we'll all be there to stand by him.

319
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:30,197
Are you accusing me of faking
all my psychic abilities?

320
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:34,600
Next time, make sure that you read
the cards right, you fools. Too bad,

321
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:36,297
because I'm getting a telepathic vision

322
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:39,100
right now that's just
guaranteed to come true.

323
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:40,752
You know you're a fraud.

324
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,200
We'll see who's a fraud when I win.

325
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:45,860
And when you, you lose in disgrace.

326
00:16:46,180 --> 00:16:47,120
Dream on, pal.

327
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,880
I don't need to dream.

328
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:52,712
Even without my psychic
abilities, I've never lost a duel.

329
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:56,918
And I can tell that's not going to
change any time in the near future.

330
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:59,657
Esper, I don't have psychic powers.

331
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:04,280
But I do have a belief in myself that
a chump like you'd never understand

332
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:08,477
Very poetic But you'll
need more than a belief to

333
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,678
stop me from blasting you
right out of the tournament

334
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:17,860
Come on,

335
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:21,217
Joey I'm tired of yapping
about the future Let's finish

336
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:26,000
this duel here and now I predict
a nasty end for you, Wheeler

337
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:27,600
Rumor has it,

338
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:31,876
without Yugi to help you You couldn't
duel your way out of a paper bag.

339
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:33,240
We'll see about that.

340
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:37,277
Prepare to taste the psychic power
of my dueling deck, you amateur.

341
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,980
Bring it on, Psycho Boy.

342
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:41,840
It's Psychic.

343
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:46,020
I'll place one card face down
on the field and end my turn.

344
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:49,617
He's got no monster on
the field to hide behind,

345
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:52,437
so I can attack him head on,
just like he attacked me.

346
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:53,932
I just need a good card.

347
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,330
All right.

348
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:56,600
Come to Joey.

349
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:58,440
Yeah, yeah.

350
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,781
Let's see him wrestle this gator.

351
00:18:01,300 --> 00:18:03,060
Now I'll summon...

352
00:18:05,540 --> 00:18:06,599
Alligator's sword!

353
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:10,960
My two monsters have a total
attack strength of 3,000.

354
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,866
60 more than his life points.

355
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:14,740
Hey, Esper.

356
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:18,240
I got a vision of the
future, and you're not in it.

357
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:24,018
You're doomed once my alligator's
sword is done with your life points.

358
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:26,510
Ah!

359
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:31,340
All right.

360
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:35,014
Hey, Serenity, one more move
and Joey will win the duel.

361
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,800
You can do it, Joey.

362
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:39,117
Don't give up, fake brawl.

363
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,037
You can still win.

364
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:40,950
I know you can.

365
00:18:41,033 --> 00:18:41,960
Be careful, Joey.

366
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:43,434
Keep up your defenses.

367
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:46,440
Your turn, Swordsman of Landstar.

368
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,348
Let's finish off this fake.

369
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:52,357
If you think I'm letting you
attack me twice, you're crazy.

370
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:55,793
So now I'm going to activate
the trap card, Mind Control.

371
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,300
Uh, this can't be good.

372
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,390
Ha!

373
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:10,441
Once a monster falls into my mind trap, it
instantly becomes my brainwashed servant.

374
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:12,420
I don't get it.

375
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:16,268
Why didn't Esper spring the trap
card during my first attack?

376
00:19:16,620 --> 00:19:20,197
If Esper had sprung mind control
when Alligator Sword attacked,

377
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:23,797
he could have used the brainwashed gator
to attack Joey Swordsman of Landstar.

378
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:26,800
but he waited to use
it on Joey's Swordsman.

379
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:28,140
Come on, Joey.

380
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,757
You know what that means.

381
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,900
There's only one reason he'd wait.

382
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:34,380
He wants to sacrifice my Swordsman.

383
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:40,080
For when he does, I'll be ready for him.

384
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:45,180
I place one card face
down and end my move.

385
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:46,440
It's showtime.

386
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:50,860
I'll sacrifice your Swordsman of
Landstar and I'll summon Jinzo.

387
00:19:54,020 --> 00:19:55,960
The end is near, Wheeler.

388
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:16,180
Come on, Chrome Dome.

389
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,377
Take your best shot.

390
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:20,300
I got a trap card ready
and waiting for you. Ha!

391
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:23,197
You better hope your
face-down card isn't a trap,

392
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:26,420
Cause if it is, my next
move may disappoint you!

393
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:28,780
Show your stuff, Jinzo!

394
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,340
Ah! My trap!

395
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:37,033
With Jinzo on the field, all
your trap cards are useless!

396
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:40,180
I foresee the finish. With no defenses,

397
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:42,357
Jinzo will destroy you in no time at all

398
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:44,297
and you'll be out of
the tournament for good,

399
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:45,210
Wheeler!

400
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:47,140
I can't let him win!

401
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:57,980
You're alone

402
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:03,360
You're alone
